==Battleground==
*20 [[Squire Rel]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 1~3 seconds<sup>30f~90f</sup>.
*10 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 2~6 seconds<sup>60f~180f</sup>.
*5 [[Shibalien Elite]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 3~9 seconds<sup>90f~270f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[M. Ost]] spawns as the boss.
**10 [[Shibalien Elite]]s spawn, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
**2 [[Elder Sloth]]s spawn, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Abuse the fact that the M. Ost will usually be in front of the Elder Sloth backliners. Stack up LD units such as [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]] or [[Little Leaguer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Golfer Cat]] at the beginning of the stage to chip away at the Elder Sloth while you deal with M. Ost with units like [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]].

In 3 Crown, the Relic Doges are now so strong that you can't stack LD units anymore, and even if you could they would get wiped by buffed Elder Sloths. Instead, bring units like [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Newtone]], [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Schoolbus Nyandam]], or [[Filibuster Cat X (Special Cat)|Talented Metafilibuster]] that outrange Elder Sloth so you can chip them both down and bully the trio with [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] and [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper The Deadeye]].

